    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d745">

                <pb facs="0763" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg751"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.68/71</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-10">October 10, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Greek Minister called to see me. The Minister stated that now that the King
                    of the Hellenes and the Greek Government were established <pb facs="0764"
                        n="752" xml:id="pg752"/> in London, he hoped that a new American Minister
                    would be appointed near that Government to replace Mr. MacVeagh.</p>
                <p>I said I would be very happy to take this matter up with the President and that I
                    felt sure that the President would desire Mr. Biddle to be accredited to the
                    Greek Government. I said that as soon as I received the President’s approval I
                    would request the <hi rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> for Mr. Biddle through
                    the Minister.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d745-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d745-f1" n="33" xml:id="d745-f1-content">
                <p>President Roosevelt gave his approval, October 14, 1941, and Anthony J. Drexel
                    Biddle, Jr., was appointed Minister to Greece, November 13, 1941.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
